<!-- <html>/<body> are ignored - only <body>'s children are copied into the page. -->
<!--
    Bottom protective-marking bar placeholder (issue #175).

    Bind this file to the "webhelp.fragment.after.body" placeholder, which is
    included at the end of <body> on ALL four generated page types (main/tiles,
    topic, search results, index terms). The element below is deliberately
    EMPTY: xslt/inc/customProtection.xsl matches it in `copy_template` mode and
    either fills it with the marking text or drops it entirely, according to the
    webhelp.show.protection / webhelp.protection.text scenario parameters.

    NOTE: this sits AFTER Oxygen's own <footer class="wh_footer">, it does not
    replace it. Fi3ldMan replaces the stock footer outright, which is why the
    stock "webhelp.fragment.footer" extension point has no effect in their
    template; here the stock footer survives untouched and the marking bar is
    appended below it.

    The <html>/<body> wrapper is not decoration: Oxygen's includeCustomHTMLContent
    copies only <body>'s children when it finds that wrapper, and copies the WHOLE
    document - these comments included - when it does not.
-->
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <body>
        <footer class="wh_footer_protection"/>
    </body>
</html>
